cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Where's Fly-do?, please cite it as below. Please also cite the Male CNS connectome, which its cell counts and wiring come from (see the README's credits)."
type: software
title: "Where's Fly-do?"
abstract: "A browser game in which ten simulated fruit flies, wired with visual inputs and mushroom body connections from the Drosophila male CNS connectome, learn through dopamine-gated plasticity to find a striped figure in a crowd."
authors:
  - given-names: Aaron
    family-names: Peabody
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/apeabody007/flydo"
url: "https://apeabody007.github.io/flydo/"
keywords:
  - connectome
  - Drosophila
  - mushroom body
  - dopamine
  - associative learning
  - psychology
